            <ArticleTitle>Fever and Hip Pain: Not Always Due to a Septic Hip.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/PEC.0000000000000985</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hip pain in febrile children always raises concern for septic arthritis. Pyomyositis is a rare cause of hip pain. Because it involves muscles around the joint, it may have a similar presentation as a septic hip. This entity therefore has the potential for posing a diagnostic dilemma when physicians face a limping child with fever. We report a child who presented with fever and hip pain and has pyomyositis of the obturator internus muscle. This case underscores the need to consider the possibility of alternative etiologies in a limping child.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
